/workspace/
# What AUCTeX parses is a cache; its style directory holds styles that a
# person writes.
/auctex/*
!/auctex/style/
# Settings that a person saves on request.  Like the Custom file they stay
# in the checkout and out of a commit; unlike it, `make check-litter' lists
# them.  To keep one under version control, remove its rule and add the
# file.
/abbrev_defs
/calc.el
/eudc-options
/shadows
/strokes
/viper
# Backup files come from an Emacs without this init, which keeps its own
# under the state root; `make check-litter' lists them.  Auto-save and lock
# files belong to an editing session, and it leaves them alone.
*~
